# Set Home Here and Set EKF Origin Here, from the flight map's menu, and Point Camera Coords with
# no height of its own. Each asks the terrain for the height at a point - srtm.getAltitude, which
# reads the .hgt tiles in the srtm folder of Mission Planner's data directory - and the data
# directory here is a scratch one holding a flat tile at 584 m for SITL's field, S36E149.hgt.
#
# Set EKF Origin Here sends SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN at the point last pressed (ArduPilot ignores it
# once its origin is set). Set Home Here asks "Are you sure?", sends MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME as a
# COMMAND_INT on OK, and asks for the home position whatever the answer, as the C#'s
# getHomePositionAsync is outside its if. Before the map has been pressed the point is (0, 0),
# PointLatLng's default, which has no tile: "No SRTM data for this area". The C#'s menu is on the
# map; here the entries are the map's right-click menu, contextMenuStripMap, so the map is
# pressed first and the entry chosen after.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:58, 4592-4623, 4903-4925, 4966-4999, ExtLibs/Utilities/srtm.cs:104-275`
#
# THIS MOVES SITL'S HOME to the middle of the map - where the vehicle is while nothing else is on
# it. Needs SITL (a copter):
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-sethome.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/srtm" && python3 -c 'import sys; open(sys.argv[1], "wb").write(bytes([2, 72]) * (1201 * 1201))' "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/srtm/S36E149.hgt"
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 15

# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions
expect fly.page.overflow 0

# Press the map: that is where the entries act.
# The map first: a press before its first paint records nothing.
expect map.ready true
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.mousedown ~ ;
expect fly.menu map
hover fly-sethome-dropdown
expect fly.menu.sub fly-sethome-dropdown

click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
hover fly-sethome-dropdown
expect fly.menu.sub fly-sethome-dropdown
click fly-setekforigin
expect fly.sent ~ SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN lat=-353
expect fly.sent ~ alt=584000

# Cancel still asks for home.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
hover fly-sethome-dropdown
expect fly.menu.sub fly-sethome-dropdown
click fly-sethome
expect fly.prompt This will reset the onboard home position (effects RTL etc). Are you Sure?
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION 0,0,0,0,0,0,0

# OK moves home to the point pressed, at the tile's height, and asks for it back.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
hover fly-sethome-dropdown
expect fly.menu.sub fly-sethome-dropdown
click fly-sethome
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent ~ COMMAND_INT MAV_CMD_DO_SET_HOME 0,0,0,0 x=-353
expect fly.sent ~ z=584 frame=0; COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION 0,0,0,0,0,0,0
expect fly.mousedown.home < 2

# Point Camera Coords with only a latitude and longitude takes the terrain's height there.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-pointcameracoords
expect fly.prompt Please enter the coords 'lat;long;alt(abs)' or 'lat;long'
key minus
type 35.36;149.16
expect fly.prompt.value -35.36;149.16
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.sent COMMAND_INT MAV_CMD_DO_SET_ROI 0,0,0,0 x=-353600006 y=1491600036 z=584 frame=0
